WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.028
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC]

00:00:03.928 --> 00:00:07.120
MAN 1: Morocco,
it's off the map.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:08.650
No one would know about it.

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:11.110
This was a place where
he could test himself,

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:14.770
both physically and mentally
with a massive amount

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:16.239
of climbing.

00:00:16.239 --> 00:00:19.510
And then, he wanted to free
solo one of the big walls

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:21.400
at the end of the trip.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:23.470
He knew that the
route that he'd chosen

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:27.430
would be one of the greatest
big wall free solos in history.

00:00:30.772 --> 00:00:33.088
MAN 2: I can't wait to
sign all of this stuff.

00:00:33.088 --> 00:00:35.380
I'm so curious if we can
actually make these walls feel

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:36.630
smaller, you know?

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:38.980
TOMMY CALDWELL: Yeah.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:41.830
There's baby goats halfway
up the first pitch.

00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:43.550
That's really cute.

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:46.420
MAN 2: Tommy was really
the only possible partner

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:49.620
for the training that I was
hoping to do in Morocco.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:52.870
We all just like to climb with
somebody who climbs so fast.

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:55.780
Like, so amazing.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:57.575
Tommy Is one of the
best in the world.

00:00:57.575 --> 00:00:59.200
When I started
climbing, he was already

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.367
a hero in the climbing
world, and I looked up to him

00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:04.365
my entire life.

00:01:04.365 --> 00:01:06.070
TOMMY CALDWELL: I
think Alex and I just

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:08.080
felt like if we got
together and climbed,

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:10.510
we could do stuff that we
couldn't do on our own.

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:14.085
And from there, it evolved into
this very close friendship.

00:01:14.085 --> 00:01:15.460
They're only going
to bring in 5.

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:18.730
MAN 2: And so knowing that
he had this giant objective,

00:01:18.730 --> 00:01:23.806
my role just became to help
him survive, essentially.

00:01:23.806 --> 00:01:27.470
MAN 1: Tommy didn't
want Alex to free solo,

00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:31.410
but he knew that Alex was
going to go do it anyways.

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:34.460
So Tommy decides
that the best way

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:38.313
that he can support his
friend is to train with him.

00:01:38.313 --> 00:01:40.230
TOMMY CALDWELL: Doing
something that dangerous

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:42.690
is really about
having full confidence

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:44.250
that you will be successful.

00:01:46.878 --> 00:01:49.180
MAN 1: Alex wanted
to push himself

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:56.510
with a huge endurance
challenge, a triple linkup.

00:01:56.510 --> 00:02:01.970
To climb 3 of the biggest walls
in Tajia with Tommy in one day.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.450
It would be the
equivalent of running

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:11.415
three back-to-back marathons
at a world record pace.

00:02:11.415 --> 00:02:13.760
MAN 3: So what's
your guess on time?

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:15.285
TOMMY CALDWELL: 22 hours.

00:02:15.285 --> 00:02:16.470
MAN 3: 22.

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:18.280
MAN 2: I think like 5:00 AM.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:21.270
So that means that we'd
be doing 21 hour link-up.

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:23.010
That's my prediction.

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:23.910
MAN 3: All right.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:24.945
Let's see who's closest.

00:02:24.945 --> 00:02:28.254
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC]

00:02:29.222 --> 00:02:31.780
MAN 2: OK, lav, good to go.

00:02:36.163 --> 00:02:41.560
MAN 1: These big walls are
extraordinarily technical.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:44.560
This is 512, 513 terrain.

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:47.650
A rating of difficulty
that really only a world

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:49.483
class climber can climb.

00:02:49.483 --> 00:02:52.535
MAN 2: I remember sort of
not really loving this pitch.

00:02:52.535 --> 00:02:54.910
TOMMY CALDWELL: I don't remember
this pitch hardly at all

00:02:54.910 --> 00:02:58.340
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC]

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:14.300
[BLEEP] My finger slipped.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:15.410
But it was a hard move.

00:03:15.410 --> 00:03:17.402
The hardest move of the route.

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:23.310
I knew Alex was going to
free solo one of the routes

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:26.290
we were climbing together.

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:27.750
Thinking about
being up there, that

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:29.910
high off the ground
without a rope,

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:31.230
that's a terrifying thought.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:34.380
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC]

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.340
Oh, god.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:41.100
MAN 2: Hey, dude.

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:42.660
TOMMY CALDWELL: Oh god.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:44.900
So fun climbing like that.

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:47.190
MAN 2: Pretty solid.

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:48.360
We did 6 and 1/2.

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:50.760
TOMMY CALDWELL: 6 and 1/2.

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:54.110
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC]

